    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0304" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1210: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sevier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-08T11:00:00-04:00">January 8, 1934—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 8—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Department’s telegram No. 8, January 6, 4 p.m.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d176-f1"
                    /> Copy of nitrate bill as finally approved by Congress was forwarded by air
                    mail January 6th.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d176-f2"/> Representative of American
                    interests says the plan appears to be a workable foundation but it is not
                    certain how it will work out in reorganization of the capital structure with
                    relation to the various classes of bondholders. He adds that he is recommending
                    that no assistance through diplomatic channels be requested at present. Repeat
                    to Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sevier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
